proof.text:
We check the root-only scheme square with the canonical $\kappa_v$ of [lem-weil-pbc-comparison-pullback]. The right adjoints of $v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}
u_T^{-1}$ and $
u_{T'}^{-1}v_{\mathrm{et}}^{-1}$ agree: at etale $U/T$ both evaluate a sheaf $G$ as $G(T'	imes_TU)$, by [def-weil-pbc-site-comparison-morphism], [def-weil-pbc-direct-image] and [def-weil-proetale-inverse-image]. By [def-per-site-comparison-pullback-data], the canonical isomorphism $
u_{T'}^*v_{\mathrm{et}}^{-1}\cong v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}
u_T^*$ of [lem-weil-pbc-comparison-pullback] is defined as the adjunction mate of this sectionwise identification of direct images. With the composite adjunctions of [def-weil-pbc-composite-adjunction], [lem-weil-pbc-conjugate-iso-unit-equation] makes it the unique isomorphism carrying one composite adjunction unit to the other; $\kappa_v$ is its inverse. Take adjuncts of the two root-square arrows under these composite adjunctions. At $U$, both adjuncts send $z$ to $\mathrm{pr}_U^\sharp(z)$: on one side this is the definition [def-pur-roots-of-unity-inverse-image] after step 2; on the other it is the etale root pullback of [lem-asd-etale-finite-twist-pullback], then step 1 on $T'$. Adjunction is a bijection on maps, so the root square commutes. All maps here are $(\mathbf Z/m)$-linear by their power formulas.
